id: pm-gh1781
title: "GH-1781: secret guard reports a single-quoted reference in compact JSON, and a value of seven backslashes, as password_assignment on 2026.11.25"
description: "Follow-up to GH-1775 (fixed in 2026.11.25). Two neighbouring shapes that returned no finding on 2026.11.14 are reported as password_assignment on 2026.11.25. First, a single-quoted run-time reference inside a JSON string in compact form: title 'password': '${BUILD_PASSWORD}' followed directly by the next member; pretty JSON, a title-only object and the double-quoted twin stay clean, so the verdict depends on serialization. Second, a single-quoted value made only of backslashes: seven backslashes (an unterminated value, since the last quote is escaped) is reported where 2026.11.14 reported nothing; six stay clean and eight were already reported. Reading: the single-quoted value is not ended at its own closing quote when it sits inside a JSON string, and an escape-only value is judged as a literal secret."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: false-positive,"gh:1781",sdk,secret-guard
